From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:29:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2179/2179] soc: qcom: adsp-pwr-lmts: drop an unused include
 and say why the send blocks

rpmsg.h provides rpmsg_device_id, so the mod_devicetable.h include is
unused.

The standby message has to be sent with the blocking rpmsg_send(). The
ADSP queues no intent on this channel in advance, so glink requests one
and waits for it. With rpmsg_trysend() the suspend-time send failed with
-EBUSY on a Surface Pro 11, and the ADSP kept waking about 45 times a
second through suspend.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_adsp_pwr_lmts.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_adsp_pwr_lmts.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_adsp_pwr_lmts.c
index 5b09a9ad65dd..5564e74134af 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_adsp_pwr_lmts.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_adsp_pwr_lmts.c
@@ -12,7 +12,6 @@
  * rpmsg device. The glink edge is its parent, so it is still up here.
  */
 #include <linux/module.h>
-#include <linux/mod_devicetable.h>
 #include <linux/pm.h>
 #include <linux/rpmsg.h>
 
@@ -36,6 +35,11 @@ static int pwr_lmts_send_state(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev, u32 state)
 	};
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The ADSP queues no intent on this channel in advance, so glink has
+	 * to request one and wait for it (up to 10 s). rpmsg_trysend() fails
+	 * with -EBUSY here, and the message never reaches the ADSP.
+	 */
 	ret = rpmsg_send(rpdev->ept, &msg, sizeof(msg));
 	if (ret)
 		dev_warn(&rpdev->dev, "failed to send standby state %u: %d\n", state, ret);
